<title>GERMANY: Bonn sets new Series 121 Bobls for tap issuance.</title>
<headline>Bonn sets new Series 121 Bobls for tap issuance.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government on Tuesday began tap issuance of a new Series 121 of five-year Bobl bonds with a coupon of 4.75 percent, the Bundesbank as issuing agent said.</p>
<p>The Bobls, which are sold to private individuals, charities and other non-profit organisations, carried an initial issue price of 100.75 for a yield of 4.58 percent.</p>
<p>The bonds mature on November 20, 2001.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
